# oracle: SPC/E water box (4500 atoms, tally example data): fix shake tol 1e-7 iter 50 on the O-H bonds and H-O-H angle, run 0 (setup only): step-0 temp, pe, ecoul, evdwl, elong and press, and every per-atom position, velocity and force after setup
# oracle-inputs: w48sh_spce.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-7 abs=1e-9
# oracle-tolerance: the setup solves (per-cluster update-size stop, see the fix shake header) match native to 1e-7 relative at tol 1e-7, where the earlier global setup sweeps were off by up to 3e-3 in the forces
units		real
atom_style	full
read_data	w48sh_spce.data
pair_style	lj/cut/coul/long 12.0 12.0
kspace_style	pppm 1.0e-4
pair_coeff	1 1 0.15535 3.166
pair_coeff	* 2 0.0000 0.0000
bond_style	harmonic
angle_style	harmonic
dihedral_style	none
improper_style	none
bond_coeff	1 1000.00 1.000
angle_coeff	1 100.0 109.47
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.0 0.0 1.0
neighbor        2.0 bin
fix             1 all shake 1e-7 50 0 b 1 a 1
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ecoul evdwl elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
